      "id": 1,
      "text": "Waka began as Wawaka, founded by German settlers in 1885, with a post office opening in 1901.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waka%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1921, residents moved to the nearby railroad town of Burnside, renaming it Waka, while the post office stayed “Wawaka” until 1927.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
